### fldigi — RTTY demodulator
License: **GNU GPL, version 3 or later** (GPL-3.0-or-later). <http://www.w1hkj.com/> ·
<https://sourceforge.net/p/fldigi/fldigi/>

Nexus's RTTY receive path (`crates/tempo-core/src/rtty/demod.rs`) is **ported
from fldigi**: `src/cw_rtty/rtty.cxx` (Copyright (C) 2012 Dave Freese, W1HKJ,
and Stefan Fendt, DL1SMF; descended from Tomi Manninen, OH2BNS's gmfsk modem,
also GPL) and `src/filters/fftfilt.cxx` (Copyright (C) 2006-2008 Dave Freese,
W1HKJ). The ported design comprises the mark/space baseband mixers, the
overlap-add FFT filters with the Feher raised-cosine "enhanced Nyquist"
response (K = 1.4), the envelope/noise-follower time constants, the
SNR-optimized Automatic Threshold Correction (ATC) slicer — a design published
by Kok Chen, W7AY (<http://www.w7ay.net/site/Technical/ATC/>), followed here as
fldigi implements it — the straddle-point bit-clock recovery, and the async
character state machine. The Baudot tables in
`crates/tempo-core/src/rtty/baudot.rs` are the US-TTY tables fldigi uses on the
air. The file header carries the same attribution, and the deliberate
differences are documented there: 12 kHz sample rate (vs fldigi's 8 kHz), a
per-character soft-confidence output (fldigi discards the slicer's continuous
value), an acquire-then-freeze AFC (fldigi's is free-running), and a
matched-filter-based signal-presence squelch. fldigi is GPL-3.0-or-later and
Nexus is GPLv3-only; the ported code is incorporated by electing version 3
(see "License compatibility" below). fldigi is an independent project; Nexus
is not affiliated with or endorsed by it.

> The Nexus RTTY **transmitter** (`crates/tempo-audio/src/rtty_afsk.rs`) is
> **not** derived from fldigi. Its shaped two-oscillator AFSK generator is an
> independent implementation of the published FSK-generation analysis by Kok
> Chen, W7AY (<http://www.w7ay.net/site/Technical/RTTY%20Sidebands/sidebands.html>) —
> a paper, not source code. No W7AY or fldigi transmit code is used.

